[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Agent tools should be limited to capabilities that support defined tasks and regular operational workflows. Required tools enable the agent’s intended work, and frequently used tools that reduce hand-offs improve its routine execution. Occasionally useful unrelated tools and speculative future tools do not justify current access and unnecessarily broaden the available tool set. OpenAI’s API supports constraining a model to a predefined set of allowed tools.

