[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Risk-stratified sampling directs human review toward outputs with the greatest likelihood or cost of error—low-confidence and high-impact cases—while random sampling of routine high-confidence outputs provides an ongoing check for hidden quality issues. This preserves scalable throughput without abandoning oversight.

