[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Retrieving only the top-k passages that historically supply the needed information reduces retrieval work and the prompt context processed on each turn, while preserving routine-answer quality. Caching stable system-prompt content avoids reprocessing an unchanged prefix. Retrieval adds compute and round trips, and preserving cached context improves cache utilization.

