[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Higher reasoning effort trades increased latency and token use for deeper reasoning, so it can consume more rate-limit capacity. Model selection should be confirmed through evaluations that represent the production workload and its quality, latency, and cost requirements. The most capable model is not invariably appropriate: smaller models can be better for cost-sensitive or latency-sensitive routine work. Tiered routing appropriately directs simple requests to a lighter model and reserves a stronger model for complex requests. Announcement recency does not establish production suitability; measured performance on the target workload does.

