[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Four distinct claim-workflow domains provide clear capability boundaries for splitting the broad triage responsibility into focused agents with smaller, domain-specific tool sets. Adding a router introduces another model invocation for every request, which compounds latency rather than addressing the underlying overload created by a single agent selecting among dozens of tools. Microsoft’s agent guidance notes that tool selection degrades as agents accumulate many tools and that each delegated agent invocation adds latency.

