[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A model can retain demographic biases from its broad pretraining even when it has not been trained on an organization’s data. For an employment-screening use case, fairness evaluation should measure whether outcomes differ across protected groups before deployment. NIST guidance calls for evaluating fairness and bias and using context-specific metrics to assess performance and harms across groups.

