[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }For classification against a fixed taxonomy, a zero-shot prompt should state the allowed categories, define them clearly, and specify the required response format. This grounds the model in the intended label set and produces consistent, machine-readable routing decisions.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A stable adversarial evaluation set, scored and recorded by model version before promotion, provides a controlled regression comparison that can reveal safety-quality drift introduced by an upgrade. Anthropic recommends thoroughly testing applications with newer models before migrating to them.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Risk likelihood and impact can be estimated only after identifying the assets affected by the deployment and their sensitivity, then identifying the relevant threat actors and attack vectors. Asset sensitivity establishes the potential consequence of compromise, while threat actors and vectors define the plausible threat scenarios. Mitigation recommendations, residual-risk acceptance, and outcome documentation follow the analysis.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Regression tests detect unintended changes in previously correct behavior by evaluating the updated system against stable, known-good reference cases.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Compliance with the approved network boundary for customer financial data is a mandatory security constraint. Operational benefits such as reduced maintenance effort, lower token costs, or architectural compatibility cannot justify adopting a managed service that fails to meet that data-handling requirement.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Human review should occur after the model produces its output but before any high-impact, irreversible action, and reviewers need explicit approval criteria. This preserves meaningful oversight and enables intervention before harm or irreversible consequences occur.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Per-query token cost directly tests compliance with the defined cost ceiling. An RBAC enforcement rate measured on adversarial test cases directly tests whether authorization controls prevent unauthorized roles from accessing patient data. Claude API costs are driven by token usage, and RBAC assigns permissions to authorized users or groups.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Reproducing the behavior with the previous model version can isolate a model-version or model-routing mismatch when retrieval has remained unchanged. Reviewing the system prompt verifies that the instructions requiring answers to be grounded in retrieved content and constrained by citations have not been removed or weakened. Claude model updates can change instruction-following behavior, so Anthropic recommends testing applications when changing models.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Zero-shot classification works when labels and their definitions are clearly specified. Few-shot examples with exact schema fields reinforce the desired extraction format. Chain-of-thought should be applied only when useful for the task, not as a blanket default. Neutral comparisons with explicit criteria counter leading framing. Model behavior can vary by version, so prompts require validation after version changes.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Haiku is designed for high-volume, latency-sensitive work such as classification, extraction, and routing. Its faster, lower-cost profile suits well-defined moderation labels that do not require deep reasoning, whereas larger models or added thinking increase latency without being necessary for this workload.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Prompt caching lets recurring requests reuse an identical stable prefix, such as a policy preamble or frequently reused context, at a much lower input-processing cost while preserving the exact content supplied to the model. Caching the static policy and commonly reused historical-sales chunks therefore reduces the two largest repeatable prompt-related costs without changing the projection inputs or model tier.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Dense vector search captures semantic similarity, which supports paraphrase retrieval. Sparse lexical retrieval is strongest for exact strings, identifiers, and rare terms. Relational queries and indexes support deterministic filtering and aggregation. Hybrid retrieval combines sparse and dense approaches, giving it different retrieval and recall behavior from dense-only search. Random sampling provides no relevance guarantee, so it is not suitable for production question-answering retrieval.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A configuration comparison can reveal whether maintenance altered the system instructions or output-schema requirements that govern JSON formatting. Replaying known-good premaintenance inputs against the current configuration and inspecting the raw Claude response separates malformed model output from failures introduced by downstream parsing. Clear output-format instructions and constraints are important for consistent model formatting behavior.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude is well suited to drafting reports from semi-structured text, reviewing long documents, extracting structured clauses, identifying deviations, classifying support tickets, and explaining classifications. A sub-50-ms streaming fraud decision needs predictable, low-latency specialized scoring rather than an LLM as its primary solution. Semantic retrieval across millions of documents requires a vector index or comparable retrieval system; Claude can use retrieved results but does not replace that index.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Portability across multiple AI clients favors MCP because it provides a standardized client-server protocol that compatible hosts can use. Interaction lifecycle also determines the integration approach: direct APIs suit simple, low-latency request-response operations, while agent handoffs transfer control and preserve context for longer-running, stateful work between specialized agents.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A direct call to the existing HTTP endpoint is the simplest and lowest-latency integration for a single stateless operation. Scoped credentials enforce least-privilege access, while a persistent session protocol, custom streaming layer, or intervening agent adds complexity and latency without serving a stated requirement. Claude supports client-side tool use, in which the application executes the tool call and returns its result.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Service credentials must not be included in prompt context because they can be exposed through logging and tracing. Authorization must be enforced before a model or tool accesses restricted data; response-layer-only RBAC allows unauthorized access to occur before rendering is blocked.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Prompt caching lets repeated calls reuse a static system-prompt prefix, so cached input is billed at a lower rate and avoids reprocessing that prefix. Routing straightforward requests to a smaller, faster model lowers inference cost and response time, while reserving the larger model for complex requests preserves quality where it matters. Increasing output limits, retrieving an entire corpus, or expanding every prompt adds processing or tokens rather than directly reducing both metrics.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Instrumentation must be designed to emit the metrics and traffic dimensions needed to distinguish normal and adversarial behavior. Those measurements support the service-level indicators used to establish SLOs; an SLO in turn defines its error budget. Alert thresholds require observed baseline distributions, whereas dashboards and on-call documentation consume the resulting telemetry after the monitoring design is established.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A p95 latency target of under 800 milliseconds at the expected request volume is a measurable performance constraint that specifies how well the system must operate. Field extraction, human-editable draft generation, and ticket classification specify functions the system must perform. Microsoft defines functional requirements as what an application does and non-functional requirements as how well it performs, including latency.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A mandatory latency SLA is a feasibility constraint: Architecture X's 4.2-second average does not meet the under-3-second requirement, whereas Architecture Y's 2.1-second average does. At 2 million sessions, the annual spend is $360,000 for X and $180,000 for Y, yielding a $180,000 annual difference. The remaining decision is whether Y's quality reduction materially reduces clinical-workflow productivity enough to outweigh its compliant performance and lower cost. AWS guidance similarly calls for discarding options that do not meet workload requirements, then selecting and testing the options that satisfy latency, throughput, and response-quality requirements while evaluating their cost-performance trade-offs.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }When Tool Search is disabled, Claude Code loads all configured MCP tool definitions into the context window at startup. A large collection of MCP servers can therefore consume tens of thousands of tokens before any engineer message is entered.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }`claude mcp list` confirms whether an MCP server is configured and reports its health status, such as connected, authentication required, or failed to connect. This establishes whether the issue is registration or session connectivity before taking disruptive action; reconnecting the session can refresh the active MCP state when necessary.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Strong architectural decision records communicate both accountability and rationale. Ownership with a review cadence keeps a decision maintainable as its assumptions or conditions change, while documenting considered alternatives and their evaluation criteria makes the trade-offs and justification understandable to current and future stakeholders. Official ADR guidance calls for ownership and for recording the context, including possible solutions considered and the decision’s consequences.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }HIPAA safeguards include access controls that restrict electronic protected health information (ePHI) to authorized workforce members. When a service provider receives PHI as part of performing services, a business associate agreement (BAA) must define and restrict permitted uses and disclosures and require appropriate safeguards; PHI therefore must not be sent to a model provider for training feedback without an applicable BAA.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Implementation teams need explicit integration contracts, configuration schemas, and expected input/output shapes to build and connect components correctly. A decision log also preserves the rationale for key architectural choices and rejected alternatives, allowing the team to apply the intended trade-offs without relying on the architect.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }AI assistance integrated directly into the IDE reduces context switching and supports code generation and review at the point where development work occurs. Requiring developers to submit requests through Slack takes them out of that environment and adds workflow friction, which undermines the productivity objective.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An ADR should document not only the decision, but also the alternatives evaluated and the consequences or trade-offs accepted. This preserves the rationale needed for future review, maintenance, audits, and onboarding.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Project-scoped configuration can be committed with the repository so all contributors receive the same MCP server definitions and tool-permission baseline. Managed configuration takes precedence over user and project settings and cannot be overridden, enabling organization-wide enforcement of security and compliance policies. Credentials should be kept out of committed project settings and supplied through secure credential mechanisms or environment variables.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An outbound tool allow-list, destination restrictions, and per-call approval constrain where an agent can transmit information, mitigating data exfiltration through tool calls. Re-running a stable adversarial evaluation set after a model-version change detects behavioral regressions and silent quality drift caused by version changes.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Reducing summarization time is an efficiency gain because it lowers labor time per document. Reduced effort does not become a productivity gain until it produces measurable additional billable output or other realized output. Extra API calls that raise infrastructure spending are a solution-cost issue. Attorney correction time adds work back into the process, creating an efficiency loss that partially offsets the time saved by automated summarization.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Project-scope MCP servers are stored in the repository’s `.mcp.json` and are designed to be committed to version control, allowing all project contributors to share the same MCP server definitions. A committed project settings file can accompany that shared repository configuration.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A threat model, residual-risk register, and control-mapping table support security assurance, risk acceptance, and compliance evaluation, so Package 1 is suited to a security and compliance reviewer. Delivered capabilities and feature-level roadmap dependencies support product planning and prioritization, so Package 2 is suited to the product manager who owns the roadmap.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Assessing a sample of recent summaries establishes whether citation fabrication is a broader production-quality problem and provides evidence for deciding its scope. Reviewing the generation pipeline for citation-grounding controls identifies whether the system has effective mechanisms to tie citations to supporting sources and expose a systemic architectural gap. NIST describes systematic evaluation of factual grounding and automated citation evaluation, while Microsoft recommends validation and monitoring of retrieval and grounding components.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An effective architecture-decision presentation starts with the decision, the business outcomes it supports, and the trade-offs accepted so executive stakeholders can assess value and risk. It then supplies the technical rationale, alternatives considered, and implementation implications needed by engineering leads to validate and carry out the decision.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Robust enterprise guardrails enforce least privilege at the action boundary: a role-specific tool allow-list prevents an unauthorized tool call before it executes, rather than relying on a model instruction to decline it. Guardrail quality also needs repeatable adversarial testing and regression tracking so prompt-injection and other bypass attempts are covered and deteriorations are detected over time. OpenAI’s guidance supports limiting allowed tools and red-teaming applications against adversarial input.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A regular cadence for reassessing expectations and assumptions keeps stakeholder alignment current as deployment conditions change. Explicitly reconciling differing stakeholder positions resolves substantive conflicts instead of leaving them hidden, creating durable alignment.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An operational SLA defines an objective metric, an acceptable threshold, the time window used to evaluate compliance, and a documented consequence or response for a breach. These elements make performance measurable and establish when remediation is required.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Code gives highest priority to organization-managed settings, followed by command-line settings, project-local settings, shared project settings, and user settings. Higher-precedence settings override the same key at lower levels.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Responsible deployment requires clear disclosure of AI involvement to the people affected by the system, enabling them to understand the nature of the interaction and calibrate their reliance appropriately. A documented, accessible path to human assistance also supports oversight and escalation when the assistant cannot appropriately resolve a need. Microsoft guidance calls for clear AI disclosure for external-facing agents and visible human handoff or interaction options.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R2cqjmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Least privilege permits the read-only catalog and policy lookups needed to prepare compliant purchase-request drafts, plus the draft-write capability required to place drafts in the review queue. Direct vendor email sending exceeds the review-only responsibility, and unrelated production-database administration is unnecessary and overly privileged.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Consistent escalation depends on explicit, repeatable triggers: a defined confidence threshold, designated high-impact decision categories, classifier-based ambiguity signals, and a user request for review. These criteria enable the workflow to identify cases requiring human oversight before a potentially consequential automated decision is finalized.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Approval-rate parity alone does not determine whether error rates, such as false-positive or false-negative rates, are comparable across protected groups. Agreement with human underwriters also does not prove fairness, because the assistant can learn and perpetuate bias embedded in the human decisions used as its reference.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Code can run a pull-request review workflow and provide automated review feedback. Keeping the existing branch-protection requirement for approving human reviews preserves human control of the merge decision; GitHub branch protection can require approving reviews before pull requests are merged.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Authorization is an application-level access-control decision because it depends on the requesting user’s identity and permissions. Compliance-audit retention is also an application-level responsibility because the application must reliably record every generated summary in the firm’s audit trail. The approved Skill can centrally apply the reusable disclaimer and prohibited-language content controls. Anthropic’s guidance describes centralized authentication and audit logging as infrastructure or gateway capabilities surrounding model interactions.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A repository-committed, project-scoped CLAUDE.md stores shared conventions and architectural context persistently, allowing Claude Code sessions in that project to load the information automatically rather than requiring repeated manual explanations.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A controlled pilot requires defining the applicable team workflows and security boundaries, including which controls must be centrally managed and which belong to a project. That decision enables a project-scope baseline for shared MCP servers, permission rules, and subagents. Claude Code distinguishes centrally managed settings from shared project settings, and project-scoped MCP servers are intended for team-shared configuration. Organization-wide training, broader rollout, and post-pilot refinement follow rather than precede the pilot.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A minimal reproduction that isolates one variable at a time establishes whether a specific input, configuration, or environment condition causes the failure and yields actionable evidence. MCP servers are external operational dependencies; Claude Code documents MCP server management and status, so listing configured servers and inspecting their status can expose connection or configuration failures. Support escalation is more effective after diagnostic evidence has been gathered, while changing model temperature or immediately rolling back a version does not constitute a complete, targeted diagnostic method.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A read-only database credential and a tool list limited to read-only operations prevent unintended writes by default, while explicit human confirmation provides an approval gate before any data-changing action. This applies defense in depth and least privilege to production access. Claude Code supports restricting available tools and permission prompts for actions that require approval.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An effective executive recommendation begins with the architectural decision and then directly addresses the financial concerns of the CFO, the legal and risk concerns of the general counsel, and the technical, security, and operational concerns of the CIO. This makes the rationale relevant and actionable for each decision-maker without burying the recommendation in premature technical or cost detail.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A complete implementation handoff needs an architecture overview and ADRs to convey the system design and rationale; component contracts to define integration boundaries; an evaluation framework with a reference set to validate behavior; runbooks and an on-call playbook to support operations; and a known-limitations record to make risks and constraints explicit.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A new design cycle is needed when new requirements cannot be met within the current architecture without changing component responsibilities or core contracts. Those changes alter fundamental design boundaries rather than making a localized operational, documentation, configuration, or content update.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Source-grounding constraints, mandatory citations, and a verification step directly reduce unsupported claims by requiring response content to be traceable to and checked against the retrieved documents.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Enterprise Claude Code permissions should follow least privilege: allow only the Bash command patterns required by approved workflows and explicitly deny sensitive operations. Claude Code supports scoped `Bash(...)` allow patterns and a `--disallowedTools` mechanism, avoiding the security risk of arbitrary shell execution across all projects.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Processing three times as many purchase orders per analyst increases throughput and reduces effort per transaction within the existing workflow, which is Efficiency. Eliminating manual data-entry work and moving staff to vendor relationship management redesigns responsibilities around higher-value work, which is Transformation. A 40% API-cost overrun is a Solution Cost concern, while 11-second latency against a committed 5-second target is a Performance SLA issue. Anthropic describes automation that frees professionals for strategic work as transforming the workflow.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An architecture guide must be planned around its target audience and the information that audience needs. It must also have an outline that organizes the required content—such as the overview, components, contracts, flows, runbooks, and limitations—before individual sections are drafted.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }GDPR requires personal data to be limited to what is necessary, retained no longer than necessary, and processed by a service provider under an appropriate binding processor arrangement. Redacting unnecessary personal data, defining retention, maintaining a Data Processing Addendum, and documenting procedures for data-subject rights support these obligations. Claude Enterprise also provides configurable data-retention controls.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Tool Search supports deferred loading, which prevents deferred MCP tool descriptions from entering the model’s initial context. The tools remain available and their definitions load on demand when discovered through search, reducing initial context overhead without removing MCP capability.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Retrieved documents can carry indirect prompt-injection instructions. Treating all retrieved content as untrusted, applying classifiers or injection detection before it reaches the model, and validating outputs establishes controls at the relevant trust boundary.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A delivery team needs implementation-level guidance covering component responsibilities, contracts between components, dominant-flow sequences, configuration parameters and defaults, and operational procedures. Together, these artifacts support building, integrating, configuring, and operating the deployment.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A Claude Code pilot needs an explicit division between workflow activities where AI assistance adds value and activities that remain under human authority. It also needs the project’s operational configuration in place: MCP integrations, permission controls, specialized subagents, and persistent project instructions/context. Claude Code documents project-scoped MCP setup, permissions, subagents, and project memory as distinct configuration mechanisms that establish those capabilities and boundaries.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An Architecture Decision Record preserves the context and rationale for an architectural choice, including alternatives, decision outcome, and consequences. Its written, attributable record supports later audits and helps new team members understand why the architecture took its current form.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Role-based access control belongs at retrieval time, before retrieved documents are added to the prompt or exposed to the model. Enforcing authorization there prevents unauthorized content from entering the model context; prompt-only instructions, general refusal behavior, and post-response filtering do not provide that security boundary. Amazon Bedrock documents ACL-aware retrieval as pre-retrieval filtering that returns only documents the supplied user is permitted to access.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An output classifier can block prohibited investment-recommendation language before it is delivered, while explicit system-prompt boundaries and prescribed refusal wording direct the assistant to decline out-of-scope investment-advice requests. Anthropic guidance recommends strengthened system prompts that state legal and ethical boundaries and how to refuse, and describes filters as a way to enforce output guardrails.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A structured discovery session establishes the specific failing decision, the affected customer journey, and a measurable target outcome before solution design begins. These definitions provide the problem scope and success criteria needed to determine whether AI is appropriate and what it should support.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Adversarial instructions embedded in retrieved content can redirect an assistant to invoke an outbound tool and transmit sensitive data to an attacker-controlled endpoint. This is an indirect prompt-injection path that enables unauthorized data exfiltration.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Code applies centrally deployed managed settings above user, project, local, and command-line configuration, preventing an engineer from overriding an enforced security policy. A managed policy is therefore the appropriate scope for an organization-wide non-overridable hardening flag.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A HIPAA-eligible Anthropic deployment must be covered by an appropriate Business Associate Agreement for an approved service. Zero Data Retention and audit logging support the required handling and accountability controls, whereas consumer and personal accounts without a BAA do not provide that contractual HIPAA coverage. The deployment must also follow Anthropic’s HIPAA-specific configuration and feature limitations.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Structured discovery elicits operational, performance, and compliance constraints from stakeholders before scoping so the solution can be designed against real requirements. Production readiness also depends on explicit, measurable success criteria and failure thresholds that can serve as deployment gates. Anthropic guidance recommends defining measurable success criteria and evaluating customer-support implementations against established benchmarks.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Security and compliance review focuses on identified threats, mappings from requirements to controls, the criteria for accepting residual risk, and traceable evidence for audits. These artifacts demonstrate that the architecture addresses security obligations and can be assessed for compliance.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Effective scope management makes the delivery and timeline effects of added work explicit, while preserving the stakeholder’s underlying objective through clear alternatives such as deferring the request, removing other scope, or extending the schedule.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An effective runbook gives on-call engineers actionable procedures for common alerts, including triage and investigation guidance, escalation paths, recovery or rollback procedures, and links to the dashboards and logs needed to diagnose the service. AWS operational guidance likewise calls for a process per alert and defined escalation paths in runbooks and playbooks.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Code exposes permission rules and the `settings.json` file from which each rule originates. Its deny rules are evaluated before ask and allow rules, while settings can be supplied at managed, command-line, project-local, shared-project, and user scopes. Inspecting the active rules and their source identifies whether a specific denial is intentional or whether the narrowly scoped rule should be amended, without removing unrelated safeguards.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Claude Skills are reusable packages of procedural knowledge, including workflows, instructions, resources, and examples, and custom Skills are supported in claude.ai, the Claude API, and Claude Code. MCP servers are designed to expose external systems such as data sources and tools. A fixed authoring workflow that has no live external-system calls is therefore best represented as a Skill.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Delegation should be calibrated to the nature of the risk in the work being assigned. Financial refund decisions can carry fraud, policy-compliance, fairness, and customer-impact risks that are not determined solely by the refund amount; efficiency does not by itself justify fully autonomous approval. Anthropic’s Delegation guidance frames task allocation as a thoughtful distribution of work based on the task and the AI system’s capabilities and limitations.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Validating output against a structured schema before downstream actions constrains the data that those actions can receive. Effective AI safety also uses defense in depth: prompt-level guidance must be supplemented by runtime content checks, because no single prompt or control provides sufficient protection on its own.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A focused agenda and advance distribution of artifacts let stakeholders prepare meaningful input. Recording decisions and follow-up actions, then confirming owners and due dates, creates shared accountability and ensures feedback is acted on.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Executive-level architectural communication should focus on the business outcomes enabled by the decision, the significant trade-offs involved, and the high-level risks that require awareness or sponsorship.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Project scope stores repository-level configuration that can be version-controlled and shared with all collaborators. User and local scopes are personal or machine-specific, so they cannot reliably enforce a common MCP server set, permissions, and project context across a team.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Actionable requirements require clarifying the people involved, the events that initiate escalation, the desired definition of successful resolution, and applicable nonfunctional constraints such as latency, cost, auditability, and data sensitivity. These details turn a vague solution request into scoping and design requirements.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Grounded documentation requires agents to inspect the relevant repository code through filesystem and code-search tools, so the content reflects the current implementation. Routing generated changes through the normal review workflow preserves human oversight and the team’s established quality controls.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Project-scoped MCP servers are stored in `.mcp.json` and committed to version control so teammates receive the same tools. Shared project settings can likewise provide team permission rules. Managed settings are the appropriate scope for security and compliance requirements because they take precedence over personal, project, and local settings and cannot be overridden by individual engineers.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Caching a stable, repeated prompt prefix allows its input tokens to be billed at the lower cached-input rate where supported, and restricting retrieval to query-relevant spans reduces the number of input tokens sent on each request. Together, these measures directly reduce the repeated-prompt and retrieved-context costs.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }System prompts should give consistent, unambiguous instructions. Removing or rewriting the instruction to fill gaps ensures the model does not invent unsupported information and remains constrained to content supported by the supplied source.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }An evaluation set should represent the relevant population and the conditions in which the system will be deployed. Testing only one region and one tenure band cannot establish reliable or equitable performance for the broader hiring population; expanding the set and rescoring before wider release provides evidence across the intended coverage.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A valid experiment is designed before assignment by defining the hypothesis and primary success metric, then planning statistical power. The minimum detectable effect and required sample size determine whether the experiment can reliably detect a meaningful difference. Result analysis, release decisions, and documentation occur after data has been collected.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Regulatory applicability must be established from the data types, jurisdiction, and audience before clause-level analysis can be scoped. The vendor’s available compliance tooling and enabled compliance affordances must also be identified so the actual controls and data-handling capabilities can be mapped to the applicable clauses. Gap analysis, remediation planning, and sign-off follow that mapping.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A deployed LLM system should retain its evaluation framework and use operational telemetry, sampled output quality, and user or stakeholder feedback to prioritize the most valuable improvement. The planned change can then be measured against defined success criteria and the established evaluation set, enabling evidence-based iteration.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Business goals, measurable success criteria, scope, and the intended user population define the outcome the capability must serve. Non-functional constraints such as latency, cost, auditability, data sensitivity, and regulatory obligations bound which solutions are acceptable. These inputs must be elicited before stakeholders can meaningfully validate the requirements.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Least privilege requires granting only the specific capabilities needed to perform the defined duties. A per-role allow-list that permits only the knowledge-base read tool and the draft-queue write tool, enforced by the orchestration layer, prevents access to unrelated tools while retaining the required functionality.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A compliance-owned Claude Skill centralizes the approved procedure as a reusable, governed workflow. Referencing that same Skill from all three integrations keeps the customer-service, sales, and onboarding implementations aligned and lets compliance updates propagate from one maintained source. Anthropic documents Skills as a way to distribute approved, standardized workflows consistently, including organization-wide management and updates.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Measured p50 and p95 latency compared with agreed SLA thresholds provides an objective, shared view of actual performance. If production constraints make the current targets unattainable, collaboratively revising the SLA realigns the service commitment with feasible performance expectations. Latency is a standard service-level indicator that may be evaluated using percentiles, and published service objectives set user expectations.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A dedicated subagent is appropriate for recurring specialist work that needs a tightly scoped system prompt, restricted tool permissions, and optionally a distinct model. Custom Claude Code subagents are reusable and can be configured with their own system prompt, tool access, and model.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A human-in-the-loop validation design must identify the pipeline decisions that warrant human oversight according to their impact and reversibility, and define the sampling and escalation criteria for each oversight point. Those controls establish the scope and behavior to be tested in the pilot; revisions based on pilot findings occur afterward.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Federated authorship enables each team to create and maintain Skills for its own domain, distributing the authoring workload. A central review and publication gate ensures that shared Skills meet organization-wide quality, security, consistency, and trust requirements before they become broadly available.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A continuous deployment lifecycle uses a persistent evaluation framework and reference set so results remain comparable across iterations and regressions can be detected. It also incorporates lessons learned from each phase into the next phase, enabling systematic improvement. Microsoft guidance describes continuously operationalized evaluation and recommends postmortems to capture deployment lessons.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }User-scope settings apply to one person across every project on that person’s machine and are intended for personal preferences such as a theme. A personal preferred response language used across all repositories therefore belongs at user scope. Organization-wide restrictions require managed settings, shared repository MCP endpoints require shared project configuration, and credentials should remain in private, uncommitted local configuration.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }A complete deployment handoff package documents the overall architecture and component design, records architectural decisions, provides runbooks for routine operations and an on-call playbook for support, and identifies known limitations for operators and future maintainers.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Per-user OAuth tokens replace a shared credential with individually attributable, scope-limited access. Including the initiating user’s identity in tool-call logs establishes accountability and an audit trail for each action.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R17ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }Input preparation reduces or condenses conversation and retrieved context before it is assembled. Prompt construction determines the ordering and stable cacheable prefix of the prompt. Output handling validates generated structured data and persists validated results for downstream use and auditing.

[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-yellow) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, #000); color: #ffffff; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-green) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, #fff); color: #172033; }
[data-question-highlight-id="question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb"]::highlight(question-marker-R16ajmlfiv5tpfiv5uadb-pink) { background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, #fff); color: #172033; }User-provided text must be treated as untrusted and cannot confer privileges or override higher-priority safety rules. Layered mitigations—prompt instructions, runtime detection of override attempts, least-privilege tool permissions that user content cannot elevate, and audit logging—reduce both the likelihood and impact of prompt-injection attempts.

